            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac rupture following intracoronary streptokinase.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thrombolytic dissolution of coronary artery thrombus has added new dimensions to early myocardial infarction treatment. Reperfusion via streptokinase infusion has been shown to be beneficial; however, adverse effects are being noted. We present the case of a patient so treated who subsequently developed left ventricular free wall rupture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
